course: dictionary
lesson: 2754
title: Feeling let down
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Disappointment is the sad feeling you get when something you hoped for does not happen, or is not as good as you expected. Context gives you clues: «Disappointment is the feeling when things turn out worse than you hoped.» The words worse than you hoped tell you what it means.
explain: Disappointment is a noun, and it is usually uncountable, so you say feel disappointment or with disappointment. A disappointment, with a and an s on the end, is a thing that lets you down. «The cancelled trip was a big disappointment.» Here it means the trip itself was not as good as hoped.
explain: Check the meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «To my disappointment, the match was called off.» Put in your meaning: To my sad feeling of being let down, the match was called off. It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Disappointment means the sad feeling when something you hoped for does not happen.
fact: A disappointment is a thing or event that is not as good as you hoped, such as a burnt cake or a cancelled trip.
fact: Useful phrases include «to my disappointment», «a big disappointment», «hide your disappointment» and «feel disappointment».
fact: «Shucks!» is an old-fashioned American word that people say instead of a rude word when they feel mild disappointment.
fact: «Bummer» is older US slang for a disappointment, and «mid» is young slang for not very good.
exercise: «Disappointment is the feeling when things turn out worse than you hoped.» What is disappointment? | A loud noise in the night | *A sad feeling when something you hoped for does not happen | A kind of cake | A prize you win for running fast
exercise: «To my disappointment, the football match was cancelled.» What does to my disappointment tell you? | The writer scored a goal | Nobody cared about the match | *The writer felt let down | The match was won by the writer
exercise: «Shucks!» is an old-fashioned American word. Why might someone say it? | To ask for a drink | *To show mild disappointment, instead of a rude word | To say hello to a friend
test: «The burnt cake was a disappointment, but Mia baked another one the next day.» What does a disappointment mean here? | *A thing that was not as good as hoped | A party with lots of guests | Winning a prize | A kind of cake
test: Which is the best way to cope with disappointment, as the lessons suggest? | Blame everyone around you | Stop wanting anything at all | Never speak of it again | *Talk about it, try again, and look for the good
exam: «Disappointment usually fades over days or weeks.» What does this suggest? | It is a kind of sport | *It is a feeling that gets smaller with time | It only happens to adults | It lasts forever
